sparse"},{"concept_id":"ear_disease","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":0.99,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"hemorrhoids","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.72,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.46,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"tinea","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":9,"lift":3.47,"evidence_tier":"studied"},{"concept_id":"wounds","dsc":1,"cul":0,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":6,"lift":0.95,"evidence_tier":"studied"}],"lead_score":0.5948},"texts":{"dsc:1.121":{"ref":"De materia medica 1.121","headword":"κοκκυμηλέα δένδρον ἐστὶ","lang":"grc","source":"dioscorides","text":"κοκκυμηλέα δένδρον ἐστὶ γνώριμον, οὗ ὁ καρπὸς ἐδώδιμος, κακοστόμαχος, κοιλίας μαλακτικός· τῶν δὲ Συριακῶν καὶ μάλιστα τῶν ἐν Δαμασκῷ γεννωμένων ὁ καρπὸς ξηρανθεὶς εὐστόμαχος καὶ κοιλίας σταλτικός. τὸ δὲ ἀφέψημα τῶν φύλλων ἐν οἴνῳ σκευαζόμενον καὶ ἀναγαργαριζόμενον κιονίδα καὶ οὖλα καὶ παρίσθμια ῥευματιζόμενα σνέλλει. τὰ δὲ αὐτὰ παρέχει καὶ ὁ τῶν ἀγρίων κοκκυμηλέων καρπὸς πέπειρος ξηρανθείς, ἑψηω δὲ μετὰ ἑψήματος εὐστομαχώτερος καὶ σταλτικώτερος κοιω γίνεται. τὸ δὲ κ όμμ ι τῆς κοκκυμηλέας ἐστὶ κολλητικόν, λίθων θρυπτικὸν πινόμενον σὺν οἴνῳ, σὺν ὄξει δὲ ἐπιχριόμενον λειχῆνας τοὺς ἐπὶ παιδίων θεραπεύει.","spans":[{"start":56,"end":66,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"adverse"},{"start":70,"end":82,"concept_id":"constipation","polarity":"action"},{"start":163,"end":171,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":178,"end":195,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":265,"end":271,"concept_id":"sore_throat","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":277,"end":281,"concept_id":"mouth_gums","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":286,"end":293,"concept_id":"sore_throat","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":416,"end":424,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":498,"end":506,"concept_id":"wounds","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":510,"end":521,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":571,"end":577,"concept_id":"dermatitis","polarity":"therapeutic"}]},"cul:239-plums":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Plums","headword":"Plums","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"All Plums are under Venus, and are like women, some better, and some worse. As there is great diversity of kinds, so there is in the operation of Plums, for some that are sweet moisten the stomach, and make the belly soluble; those that are sour quench thirst more, and bind the belly; the moist and waterish do sooner corrupt in the stomach, but the firm do nourish more, and offend less. The dried fruit sold by the grocers under the names of Damask Prunes, do somewhat loosen the belly, and being stewed, are often used, both in health and sickness, to relish the mouth and stomach, to procure appetite, and a little to open the body, allay choler, and cool the stomach. Plum-tree leaves boiled in wine, are good to wash and gargle the mouth and throat, to dry the flux of rheum coming to the palate, gums, or almonds of the ear. The gum of the tree is good to break the stone. The gum or leaves boiled in vinegar, and applied, kills tetters and ringworms. Matthiolus saith, The oil preserved out of the kernels of the stones, as oil of almonds is made, is good against the inflamed piles, the tumours or swellings of ulcers, hoarseness of the voice, roughness of the tongue and throat, and likewise the pains in the ears. And that five ounces of the said oil taken with one ounce of muskadel, drives forth the stone, and helps the cholic.","spans":[{"start":270,"end":284,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"action"},{"start":472,"end":488,"concept_id":"constipation","polarity":"action"},{"start":597,"end":605,"concept_id":"appetite_loss","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":623,"end":636,"concept_id":"constipation","polarity":"action"},{"start":656,"end":672,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":776,"end":781,"concept_id":"common_cold","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":804,"end":808,"concept_id":"mouth_gums","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":874,"end":879,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":937,"end":944,"concept_id":"dermatitis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":949,"end":958,"concept_id":"tinea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1086,"end":1091,"concept_id":"hemorrhoids","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1121,"end":1127,"concept_id":"skin_ulcers","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1129,"end":1139,"concept_id":"sore_throat","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1154,"end":1177,"concept_id":"mouth_gums","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1207,"end":1224,"concept_id":"ear_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1314,"end":1319,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1335,"end":1341,"concept_id":"colic","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"gloss":{"dsc:1.121":{"56":"bad for the stomach (κακοστόμαχος)","70":"loosens / moves the bowels (laxative)","163":"good for the stomach (εὐστόμαχος)","178":"binds / checks the bowels","265":"(relaxed) uvula (κιονίς)","277":"the gums (οὖλα)","286":"tonsils / tonsillitis (παρίσθμια)","416":"good for the stomach (εὐστόμαχος)","498":"agglutinant, closing wounds (κολλητικός)","510":"breaks up stones (λίθους θρύπτει)","571":"lichen, tetter (λειχήν)"},"cul:239-plums":{"270":"binds the belly (astringent, antidiarrhoeal)","472":"purges / opens / loosens the belly: laxative, purgative","597":"appetite (provokes / restores)","623":"purges / opens / loosens the belly: laxative, purgative","656":"weak / cold / hot stomach (dyspepsia)","776":"rheum, thin rheums: catarrhal discharge","804":"gums (sore, spongy, bleeding)","874":"the stone (urinary calculus)","937":"tetters: vesicular or scaly eruptions (eczema, herpes)","949":"ringworm","1086":"piles: haemorrhoids","1121":"ulcers (old, foul, running, fretting)","1129":"hoarseness of the throat / voice","1154":"roughness of the tongue","1207":"pains / noise / singing / worms in the ears","1314":"the stone (urinary calculus)","1335":"cholic: colic, griping abdominal pain"}},"images":[]}